1
00:00:00,053 --> 00:00:01,972
-See ya.
-See you tomorrow.

2
00:00:04,016 --> 00:00:05,308
Hmm? Oh.

3
00:00:06,393 --> 00:00:07,811
There's Junta.

4
00:00:07,894 --> 00:00:09,730
He's working hard, as usual.

5
00:00:10,564 --> 00:00:12,899
Maybe I could watch him practice.

6
00:00:12,983 --> 00:00:14,818
Hey. No, wait a minute.

7
00:00:15,318 --> 00:00:16,778
-That's a bad idea.
-Hey!

8
00:00:16,862 --> 00:00:18,447
-I need to avoid anything…
-Mm… Ah!

9
00:00:18,530 --> 00:00:20,490
…that lets Riri plot something
at all costs.

10
00:00:20,574 --> 00:00:21,950
Are you okay?

11
00:00:22,034 --> 00:00:23,827
I could end up dead!

12
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:26,830
Um… Hm!

13
00:01:57,796 --> 00:02:01,091
#9 GINGER ALE IS A FORCE MAJEURE

14
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,218
Now that I think about it,

15
00:02:03,301 --> 00:02:06,805
the baseball club manager's
actually really cute.

16
00:02:07,514 --> 00:02:10,642
I wonder if he'd ever date
someone like her.

17
00:02:10,725 --> 00:02:13,478
Maybe, if he weren't under Riri's spell.

18
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:17,899
I feel terrible getting him involved
in this whole messed up situation.

19
00:02:18,567 --> 00:02:19,401
-Here.
-Ah…

20
00:02:19,484 --> 00:02:22,612
Your attention, please.
Doors' opening on the right.

21
00:02:22,696 --> 00:02:24,823
Huh? Anzu?

22
00:02:24,906 --> 00:02:25,740
Huh?

23
00:02:27,284 --> 00:02:28,451
Yeah, it is.

24
00:02:28,994 --> 00:02:30,704
Amin, Riporin!

25
00:02:30,787 --> 00:02:32,914
Wow, how have you been, Anzu?

26
00:02:33,498 --> 00:02:36,042
We were just talking
about how we should have a reunion.

27
00:02:36,126 --> 00:02:37,669
Really? That'd be fun!

28
00:02:37,752 --> 00:02:39,796
We'll invite whoever we can contact.

29
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:42,424
Hey, are you busy now?
Let's go have tea.

30
00:02:42,507 --> 00:02:44,259
That sounds great. Let's go!

31
00:02:44,342 --> 00:02:45,343
Any ideas where?

32
00:02:45,427 --> 00:02:46,928
Let's do Zarigariya.

33
00:02:48,722 --> 00:02:51,808
Amin, I haven't seen you
since elementary school,

34
00:02:51,892 --> 00:02:54,394
but Riporin, we saw each other
at the station, remember?

35
00:02:54,477 --> 00:02:56,563
Yeah, that was ages ago.

36
00:02:56,646 --> 00:02:59,149
We couldn't even exchange contact info,

37
00:02:59,232 --> 00:03:01,359
because you didn't have a phone back then.

38
00:03:01,443 --> 00:03:03,445
Yeah, my parents waited to get me a phone,

39
00:03:03,528 --> 00:03:05,447
because I would just play games all day.

40
00:03:05,947 --> 00:03:07,866
No way. Well, it's true.

41
00:03:07,949 --> 00:03:10,994
You did spend all of your time
playing video games with the boys.

42
00:03:11,077 --> 00:03:13,872
That's true. And you guys played
some of the scary games.

43
00:03:14,456 --> 00:03:15,874
Oh, like Cat Ranger.

44
00:03:15,957 --> 00:03:19,211
Tonta and I were the only ones
who played it in the beginning.

45
00:03:19,711 --> 00:03:20,921
Tonta?

46
00:03:21,004 --> 00:03:22,631
Oh yeah, he was that, um,

47
00:03:22,714 --> 00:03:25,091
chubby kid with the, the wild hair.

48
00:03:25,175 --> 00:03:28,136
What? I don't remember.
What's his last name?

49
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:30,055
What? His last name?

50
00:03:30,639 --> 00:03:34,142
Um, Tonta, um, Ton…

51
00:03:34,726 --> 00:03:36,937
You hung out so much,
how could you forget?

52
00:03:38,313 --> 00:03:41,191
Now let's see.
There was a "mi" in his last name.

53
00:03:41,733 --> 00:03:44,402
Hm, it's… Oh, that's right.

54
00:03:44,486 --> 00:03:45,862
It's Junta Hayami.

55
00:03:46,363 --> 00:03:47,405
What?

56
00:03:48,782 --> 00:03:51,993
What? What?

57
00:03:52,494 --> 00:03:55,413
How awesome, I got it. Hayami, was it?

58
00:03:55,497 --> 00:03:57,707
I wonder what he's up to these days.

59
00:03:57,791 --> 00:03:58,875
Hayami?

60
00:03:58,959 --> 00:04:01,419
Um, well,
I still can't remember that name.

61
00:04:02,545 --> 00:04:05,465
Hey, isn't that
a Cat Ranger character?

62
00:04:06,007 --> 00:04:07,634
Tonta, do you play too?

63
00:04:07,717 --> 00:04:09,010
Huh, mm-hm.

64
00:04:09,094 --> 00:04:11,930
For real? All right, let's play.

65
00:04:12,764 --> 00:04:14,307
I have been wanting to play in team mode

66
00:04:14,391 --> 00:04:17,060
and Ryuya and those guys don't play.
They're so boring.

67
00:04:17,644 --> 00:04:18,895
Come to my place!

68
00:04:18,979 --> 00:04:20,605
What? Really, Miss Hoshino?

69
00:04:20,689 --> 00:04:21,940
Call me Anzu.

70
00:04:22,691 --> 00:04:24,442
Okay, Miss Anzu.

71
00:04:24,526 --> 00:04:26,528
You can leave out the "Miss", okay?

72
00:04:28,697 --> 00:04:29,948
Tonta's…

73
00:04:30,782 --> 00:04:32,158
Junta?

74
00:04:32,242 --> 00:04:34,661
Anzu, you look like
you just ate a bee hive.

75
00:04:34,744 --> 00:04:36,329
Do you have a stomachache?

76
00:04:36,913 --> 00:04:40,208
I can't believe how stupid I am.
I could just die.

77
00:04:40,292 --> 00:04:41,835
Well, what happened?

78
00:04:41,918 --> 00:04:45,839
Uh, Tonta wasn't his real name.
It's a nickname.

79
00:04:45,922 --> 00:04:49,092
Jeez, when I think about it now,
it's totally obvious.

80
00:04:49,175 --> 00:04:53,054
I mean, what kind of jerk doesn't know
their friend's real name?

81
00:04:53,138 --> 00:04:55,307
He's not like some rando from online.

82
00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:56,516
Next up, Hayami.

83
00:04:56,599 --> 00:04:57,600
Oh, yes.

84
00:04:57,684 --> 00:05:01,271
But to be fair,
Junta has changed dramatically.

85
00:05:01,354 --> 00:05:03,857
He's totally unrecognizable from before.

86
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:05,108
Anzu?

87
00:05:05,817 --> 00:05:10,196
Tonta, I mean Junta,
goes to the same school as me now.

88
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:11,823
Oh, really, he does?

89
00:05:11,906 --> 00:05:14,576
Did you forget him
because he's kind of quiet?

90
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:17,829
Well, he's had a dramatic transformation.

91
00:05:17,912 --> 00:05:20,498
Like an amoeba to an elephant.

92
00:05:20,582 --> 00:05:22,667
That's like an entirely different species.

93
00:05:23,251 --> 00:05:25,295
Seriously? We have to see him.

94
00:05:25,378 --> 00:05:26,796
Yeah, I'm totally curious.

95
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:28,465
-Call him!
-Call him!

96
00:05:28,548 --> 00:05:31,092
Um… I guess I could give it a try,

97
00:05:31,176 --> 00:05:33,386
but he'll probably be tired from baseball.

98
00:05:39,059 --> 00:05:40,310
Hey, how's it going?

99
00:05:42,896 --> 00:05:44,230
Who's this?

100
00:05:44,314 --> 00:05:46,358
You are a different species!

101
00:05:46,441 --> 00:05:49,319
Please be quiet. You're way too loud.

102
00:05:49,402 --> 00:05:51,446
Tonta's an athlete now?

103
00:05:51,529 --> 00:05:53,073
And he's hot!

104
00:05:53,156 --> 00:05:56,076
What happened
with all of your signature wild hair?

105
00:05:56,159 --> 00:05:58,328
It's still curly when it grows out.

106
00:05:58,912 --> 00:06:01,498
You're, um, Sayuki and, um, Igawa?

107
00:06:01,581 --> 00:06:02,832
-Riporin.
-Amin.

108
00:06:02,916 --> 00:06:04,000
Be less formal!

109
00:06:04,501 --> 00:06:06,586
-I mean, we can be casual.
-Mm-hm.

110
00:06:06,669 --> 00:06:09,339
We're talking about
having a reunion next Saturday.

111
00:06:09,422 --> 00:06:10,507
You'll come, right?

112
00:06:10,590 --> 00:06:12,300
Huh? A reunion?

113
00:06:12,967 --> 00:06:14,594
Anzu, are you gonna go?

114
00:06:15,178 --> 00:06:16,846
Well yeah, I was planning on it.

115
00:06:16,930 --> 00:06:19,307
I can't wait to see everyone's faces.

116
00:06:19,391 --> 00:06:21,810
We need everyone from school to see this

117
00:06:21,893 --> 00:06:24,354
and to understand
that Tonta the bashful, I mean,

118
00:06:24,437 --> 00:06:25,897
Junta, became an athlete.

119
00:06:26,898 --> 00:06:28,441
Sure, if Anzu is.

120
00:06:28,525 --> 00:06:31,820
Oh yeah, I have a game that day
so I might be late.

121
00:06:31,903 --> 00:06:32,946
No prob.

122
00:06:33,029 --> 00:06:34,155
I'm excited.

123
00:06:34,656 --> 00:06:37,200
Are you sure? You're so busy.

124
00:06:37,784 --> 00:06:39,035
Nah, I'll be all right.

125
00:06:39,619 --> 00:06:42,872
But, usually you practice more
once you get home.

126
00:06:42,956 --> 00:06:45,125
And then you walk me back from work too.

127
00:06:45,208 --> 00:06:47,794
So, how long have you guys been dating?

128
00:06:47,877 --> 00:06:48,920
-Huh?
-Huh?

129
00:06:49,003 --> 00:06:51,464
No! It's not like that!

130
00:06:51,548 --> 00:06:54,050
It does make sense
that you're with him.

131
00:06:54,134 --> 00:06:56,469
Seriously, girl,
you've got a great eye.

132
00:06:56,553 --> 00:06:59,222
-Are we having fun?
-Oh, chill.

133
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:07,814
This is unbelievable. Junta really
was my childhood friend, Tonta.

134
00:07:07,897 --> 00:07:08,940
So does that mean

135
00:07:09,023 --> 00:07:12,986
it's not just a spell,
and he actually does like me?

136
00:07:13,069 --> 00:07:17,574
Junta's had a secret crush on you
since elementary school!

137
00:07:17,657 --> 00:07:18,950
Don't do this to him!

138
00:07:19,701 --> 00:07:21,202
Now that I know…

139
00:07:22,370 --> 00:07:24,080
-Hmm?
-Hmm.

140
00:07:24,789 --> 00:07:26,749
Uh, ugh!

141
00:07:28,251 --> 00:07:31,921
I want to crawl under a rock
of blissful ignorance.

142
00:07:32,005 --> 00:07:34,757
So, um, sounds like
you're a bit overwhelmed right now.

143
00:07:34,841 --> 00:07:35,842
What's going on?

144
00:07:41,806 --> 00:07:43,475
Ta-da!

145
00:07:44,058 --> 00:07:47,562
Yay! I am so excited for the reunion!

146
00:07:47,645 --> 00:07:50,648
And don't even think
about wearing your normal frumpy clothes.

147
00:07:50,732 --> 00:07:51,983
I'll pick out your outfit.

148
00:07:54,068 --> 00:07:56,946
What's going on here, Riri?

149
00:07:57,030 --> 00:07:58,990
Whatever do you mean?

150
00:08:00,617 --> 00:08:02,243
Junta was really Tonta.

151
00:08:02,327 --> 00:08:05,455
I thought he was an old friend
you made up using magic.

152
00:08:06,456 --> 00:08:07,999
-You bonehead.
-Huh?

153
00:08:08,082 --> 00:08:11,503
I never ever ever told you
that I made him up now, did I?

154
00:08:12,462 --> 00:08:16,508
You just didn't recognize him at all
because he had transformed so much.

155
00:08:17,133 --> 00:08:21,304
Yeah, but didn't you cast a spell on Junta
so he would fall in love with me?

156
00:08:21,387 --> 00:08:24,015
It's not a spell.
I had nothing to do with it.

157
00:08:24,098 --> 00:08:26,351
Junta genuinely
has feelings for you,

158
00:08:26,434 --> 00:08:28,603
-and magic isn't even a factor.
-What?

159
00:08:29,103 --> 00:08:32,857
Emotional manipulation
of our subjects is absolutely forbidden

160
00:08:32,941 --> 00:08:34,234
-among wizards.
-Huh?

161
00:08:34,317 --> 00:08:37,445
If that were allowed,
I would have cast a spell on you by now.

162
00:08:38,613 --> 00:08:39,572
That's true.

163
00:08:39,656 --> 00:08:43,535
I just shorten the amount of time
it would take for you to reunite.

164
00:08:43,618 --> 00:08:45,286
What does that mean?

165
00:08:45,370 --> 00:08:48,456
Well, for example,
at your high school orientation,

166
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:51,125
Junta saw you
and he even tried to talk to you.

167
00:08:51,209 --> 00:08:52,418
What, he did?

168
00:08:52,502 --> 00:08:54,462
-Anzu, I'm here. Let's go.
-Huh?

169
00:08:55,630 --> 00:08:58,091
However, Miss Gamer,
what do you think you did?

170
00:08:58,174 --> 00:09:01,052
Huh, uh, I don't remember what I…

171
00:09:01,135 --> 00:09:03,846
Why don't we have lunch together
before we head home?

172
00:09:03,930 --> 00:09:07,642
Ah! I needed to use a recovery spell
to win the game!

173
00:09:07,725 --> 00:09:09,811
-Uh, hurry, let's go home.
-What?

174
00:09:09,894 --> 00:09:12,855
Hey Anzu, what about lunch?
Aren't you hungry?

175
00:09:12,939 --> 00:09:14,607
Finishing the game is priority one.

176
00:09:14,691 --> 00:09:17,151
Oh good grief, Anzu!

177
00:09:19,404 --> 00:09:20,613
Oh yeah.

178
00:09:20,697 --> 00:09:23,866
I was just about to finish a game,
so I ran home to play it.

179
00:09:23,950 --> 00:09:24,951
That's right.

180
00:09:25,034 --> 00:09:29,163
Splendidly, flawlessly, foolishly,
you completely ignored him.

181
00:09:29,747 --> 00:09:31,624
And once you started school…

182
00:09:32,208 --> 00:09:35,003
you would always rush straight home
as soon as classes ended,

183
00:09:35,086 --> 00:09:36,629
so you could play your games!

184
00:09:38,006 --> 00:09:39,841
It was like you were trying
to set a record

185
00:09:39,924 --> 00:09:41,634
for who could get home the fastest.

186
00:09:41,718 --> 00:09:42,635
Uh…

187
00:09:42,719 --> 00:09:44,137
And in Junta's case,

188
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:46,014
he keeps missing the chance
to talk to you,

189
00:09:46,097 --> 00:09:48,224
because baseball has him so busy.

190
00:09:49,475 --> 00:09:50,602
Huh?

191
00:09:51,936 --> 00:09:53,187
First-years, gather!

192
00:09:56,733 --> 00:10:00,695
So I cut off the reunion,
because you two were taking too damn long!

193
00:10:00,778 --> 00:10:02,155
You can't just cut it!

194
00:10:03,740 --> 00:10:06,492
All of it is to help you
find love, Anzu.

195
00:10:06,576 --> 00:10:08,286
Ugh, it's none of your business!

196
00:10:08,369 --> 00:10:09,871
I don't care anymore!

197
00:10:09,954 --> 00:10:12,498
Just give me back
my three greatest desires!

198
00:10:12,582 --> 00:10:13,416
That hurts!

199
00:10:13,499 --> 00:10:15,126
If I do nothing,

200
00:10:15,209 --> 00:10:19,756
then your dictionary will have
no entry included for romance.

201
00:10:19,839 --> 00:10:20,923
I surrender, I surrender.

202
00:10:21,007 --> 00:10:22,425
VIDEO GAMES: VERY FUN. CHOCOLATE:
DELICIOUS. CAT: FLUFFY AND CUTE.

203
00:10:23,134 --> 00:10:26,346
Ugh, could any romance replace
the three things I love most?

204
00:10:26,429 --> 00:10:29,098
But you're the Anti-Heroine,
how could you say that?

205
00:10:29,182 --> 00:10:30,099
Ugh…

206
00:10:30,183 --> 00:10:33,227
With girls like you,
we have to be a bit more aggressive,

207
00:10:33,811 --> 00:10:36,356
or you'll keep missing
great opportunities.

208
00:10:39,067 --> 00:10:41,611
-And die alone!
-Jeez, harsh much?

209
00:10:41,694 --> 00:10:44,989
Hold on, why am I the only one
being treated like an outcast?

210
00:10:45,782 --> 00:10:48,117
Saki has no interest in dating either.

211
00:10:48,618 --> 00:10:52,205
That's because Saki is
already insanely popular.

212
00:10:53,247 --> 00:10:55,291
Saki, please, I love you so much!

213
00:10:55,375 --> 00:10:57,168
So she won't need help
finding someone.

214
00:10:57,251 --> 00:10:58,294
SAKI LOVE

215
00:10:59,545 --> 00:11:03,049
I'm so sorry, for even considering
I'm in the same league as her.

216
00:11:03,132 --> 00:11:05,426
Now, do you understand it, huh?

217
00:11:05,510 --> 00:11:07,053
What we're doing, Anzu,

218
00:11:07,136 --> 00:11:10,264
is a romantic relationship project
to help you find a love

219
00:11:10,348 --> 00:11:12,809
that surpasses your love
for your greatest desires.

220
00:11:14,268 --> 00:11:16,479
Well, I say screw that project.

221
00:11:17,689 --> 00:11:20,566
But anyway, even if Tonta is Junta,

222
00:11:20,650 --> 00:11:23,027
the fact remains
that the two of us are just friends.

223
00:11:24,237 --> 00:11:25,113
Heh?

224
00:11:26,155 --> 00:11:27,407
Huh?

225
00:11:27,490 --> 00:11:29,158
Um, hmm?

226
00:11:29,659 --> 00:11:31,786
Get out!

227
00:11:31,869 --> 00:11:33,913
You kick me out now?

228
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:41,629
Hey, what happened to Tonta?

229
00:11:41,713 --> 00:11:44,090
-He left already.
-Really?

230
00:11:44,173 --> 00:11:46,884
Oh, I wanted to game with him today.

231
00:11:46,968 --> 00:11:49,637
He told me that he's sick
of playing Cat Ranger.

232
00:11:49,721 --> 00:11:50,638
Seriously?

233
00:11:50,722 --> 00:11:53,683
We were just talking about
how we wanted to beat the top score.

234
00:11:53,766 --> 00:11:55,476
You should beat it with us then!

235
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:57,186
Yeah!

236
00:11:57,270 --> 00:11:59,689
You guys didn't even want
to play Cat Ranger before.

237
00:11:59,772 --> 00:12:01,899
Hey, that's not true.

238
00:12:05,820 --> 00:12:08,156
Did you say Anzu was coming
to the reunion too?

239
00:12:08,239 --> 00:12:10,742
Anzu? Yeah, she's coming.

240
00:12:10,825 --> 00:12:13,077
Was graduation the last time you saw her?

241
00:12:13,161 --> 00:12:14,078
Yeah.

242
00:12:14,162 --> 00:12:17,081
Heh, she'll probably come
in her lame cat clothes.

243
00:12:17,165 --> 00:12:19,584
-You've got a problem with cats?
-Huh?

244
00:12:19,667 --> 00:12:21,335
-Anzu?
-Wow.

245
00:12:21,419 --> 00:12:24,964
Look at you, Anzu,
you look so cute, all dressed up.

246
00:12:25,047 --> 00:12:27,133
That's right, girlie. Rock on.

247
00:12:27,216 --> 00:12:28,301
Uh…

248
00:12:28,384 --> 00:12:31,220
Wow, Anzu's got decent clothes on, guys.

249
00:12:31,304 --> 00:12:32,847
And your hair's not everywhere.

250
00:12:32,930 --> 00:12:35,141
I'm really sorry
to disappoint you all, fellas.

251
00:12:35,725 --> 00:12:37,185
But it's only thanks to their help.

252
00:12:37,268 --> 00:12:39,979
I gotta pee! I really gotta pee!

253
00:12:40,062 --> 00:12:41,981
Please just stay still now.

254
00:12:42,064 --> 00:12:44,692
Hey, you forgot to take off the tag.

255
00:12:44,776 --> 00:12:46,652
Just because you changed a little,

256
00:12:46,736 --> 00:12:49,238
doesn't mean you can act
like you're all that.

257
00:12:49,322 --> 00:12:51,866
Clearly, you haven't changed much, Ryuya,

258
00:12:51,949 --> 00:12:53,034
especially your height.

259
00:12:53,117 --> 00:12:55,244
Hey, I'm still growing, all right?

260
00:12:55,328 --> 00:12:57,663
I mean, maybe you just grew too much!

261
00:12:58,998 --> 00:13:01,250
Hey, let's play girls against guys.

262
00:13:01,751 --> 00:13:04,170
The team
with the highest total score wins.

263
00:13:04,670 --> 00:13:07,548
There's more girls than guys,
so that sounds fair, right?

264
00:13:08,174 --> 00:13:10,134
Yeah, I'm in. Sounds like fun.

265
00:13:10,218 --> 00:13:12,136
So, what should the losers have to do?

266
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:13,846
What?

267
00:13:13,930 --> 00:13:16,933
How about, losers confess
who their first love was?

268
00:13:17,767 --> 00:13:20,645
Uh-oh, I can only think
of game characters.

269
00:13:20,728 --> 00:13:22,939
We don't expect too much
from you, Bushy.

270
00:13:23,523 --> 00:13:25,399
Well, what should we do?

271
00:13:27,026 --> 00:13:28,778
I'm on the girls' team,

272
00:13:28,861 --> 00:13:30,988
so everything is gonna be a-okay.

273
00:13:31,072 --> 00:13:31,906
MASTER OF GAMES

274
00:13:31,989 --> 00:13:32,949
Yeah!

275
00:13:33,032 --> 00:13:36,828
Huh, do you have any idea
what it means to challenge me?

276
00:13:36,911 --> 00:13:40,998
You're all merely average fools!
You have hardly won any games!

277
00:13:41,082 --> 00:13:43,584
I'll make sure
that you all know your place!

278
00:13:43,668 --> 00:13:45,711
-Anzu!
-Yay, Anzu!

279
00:13:45,795 --> 00:13:48,172
You sound just like a villain, girl.

280
00:13:48,881 --> 00:13:51,676
Don't think that this game's
going down like that!

281
00:13:51,759 --> 00:13:54,011
This isn't grade school, you'll be silly!

282
00:13:54,095 --> 00:13:55,179
You mean, "sorry."

283
00:13:59,851 --> 00:14:01,769
Nobody realizes

284
00:14:01,853 --> 00:14:03,646
that the secret to winning in bowling…

285
00:14:04,564 --> 00:14:07,608
is that you first have to read
the oil on the lane…

286
00:14:09,861 --> 00:14:11,946
then visualize your target.

287
00:14:13,072 --> 00:14:16,075
And finally, you inject that motivation!

288
00:14:16,158 --> 00:14:19,412
Now, prepare for death!

289
00:14:20,830 --> 00:14:23,374
Strike!

290
00:14:29,171 --> 00:14:32,466
I just got to smash Riri
so many times!

291
00:14:32,550 --> 00:14:34,093
GIRLS' TEAM WIN!

292
00:14:34,176 --> 00:14:37,513
Now, as promised,
tell us who all your first loves were.

293
00:14:37,597 --> 00:14:39,599
FIGHT ON

294
00:14:39,682 --> 00:14:41,183
And get down on your knees!

295
00:14:41,267 --> 00:14:42,852
Don't make it worse.

296
00:14:43,519 --> 00:14:44,687
Well, what can we do?

297
00:14:44,770 --> 00:14:47,440
-Let's sit down, at least.
-Uh, you go first, man.

298
00:14:48,441 --> 00:14:51,402
Um! Mine was… It was Okawa.

299
00:14:51,485 --> 00:14:52,653
Ooh!

300
00:14:53,195 --> 00:14:54,864
Mine was Yoshida.

301
00:14:56,574 --> 00:14:58,743
Mine was Amin.

302
00:15:00,244 --> 00:15:03,497
Huh, who? Me? No way.

303
00:15:03,581 --> 00:15:05,207
It's over!

304
00:15:05,291 --> 00:15:07,501
Hey, Ryuya, you're next.

305
00:15:09,086 --> 00:15:11,005
Fine. Mine was…

306
00:15:11,088 --> 00:15:14,008
Yamaguchi, you cool dude,
get a hold of yourself!

307
00:15:14,091 --> 00:15:16,594
Good thing
Junta didn't get here yet.

308
00:15:16,677 --> 00:15:19,013
I always liked Anzu!

309
00:15:19,847 --> 00:15:21,599
Come on, man.

310
00:15:22,099 --> 00:15:23,100
Hey.

311
00:15:23,809 --> 00:15:25,227
My preschool teacher.

312
00:15:25,978 --> 00:15:28,022
You've got to give us
something better than that, dude!

313
00:15:28,105 --> 00:15:29,565
Damn it!

314
00:15:29,649 --> 00:15:31,567
We won't lose again! Rematch, now!

315
00:15:31,651 --> 00:15:33,235
Again, dude? Really?

316
00:15:33,319 --> 00:15:35,488
Yamaguchi's HP is at zero.

317
00:15:36,489 --> 00:15:37,907
This is revenge!

318
00:15:37,990 --> 00:15:40,660
Come on, guys!
Let's show these girls what we've got!

319
00:15:40,743 --> 00:15:43,204
Sure, guys. I mean,
if you want to look even worse.

320
00:15:46,874 --> 00:15:49,085
Okay then, losers buy ice cream.

321
00:15:49,168 --> 00:15:51,921
Your crushes were less interesting
than I could have imagined.

322
00:15:53,422 --> 00:15:56,050
Now you just put his HP in the negative!

323
00:15:57,760 --> 00:16:00,096
Saw this coming?

324
00:16:02,682 --> 00:16:05,935
Yay! Now let's all do karaoke!

325
00:16:07,561 --> 00:16:10,147
Anzu, I challenge you to karaoke!

326
00:16:10,231 --> 00:16:11,190
Sure thing.

327
00:16:11,774 --> 00:16:13,317
Ryuya, just let it go, man.

328
00:16:13,401 --> 00:16:14,860
Hey, you know what,

329
00:16:14,944 --> 00:16:17,905
you guys really haven't changed
since grade school.

330
00:16:25,663 --> 00:16:26,539
YOU HAVE A FIRM VOICE.

331
00:16:26,622 --> 00:16:27,915
PRACTICE ADJUSTING THE PITCH
AND AIM FOR A HIGHER SCORE.

332
00:16:27,999 --> 00:16:29,792
All right. Not bad.

333
00:16:37,133 --> 00:16:37,967
PITCH AT THE BEGINNING IS PERFECT

334
00:16:38,050 --> 00:16:38,968
IT WOULD BE GOOD
IF YOU TRY TO RELAX MORE

335
00:16:39,677 --> 00:16:42,972
No! I don't believe this!

336
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:54,275
-You're such a sore loser.
-Hmph!

337
00:16:55,901 --> 00:16:58,362
Oh come on,
you losing to me is such old news.

338
00:16:58,446 --> 00:17:01,032
Anzu, you really know
how to piss me off!

339
00:17:01,115 --> 00:17:04,535
Oh, you're one to talk, Ryuya.
You're just a two-timer.

340
00:17:04,618 --> 00:17:07,079
What? You're a two-timer? Really?

341
00:17:07,163 --> 00:17:08,789
Hey, shut up!

342
00:17:08,873 --> 00:17:10,541
Yeah, but it's true.

343
00:17:10,624 --> 00:17:12,043
Oh, come on.

344
00:17:12,126 --> 00:17:15,129
Quit your moping.
Just sing a song with Anzu and cheer up.

345
00:17:15,212 --> 00:17:17,006
Oh, all right, fine.

346
00:17:19,425 --> 00:17:20,885
So, what do you wanna sing?

347
00:17:21,761 --> 00:17:22,636
YOU HAVE A NEW MESSAGE

348
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:25,014
Oh, um.

349
00:17:26,098 --> 00:17:28,017
Oh, Junta just got here.

350
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:30,352
I'll go get him.

351
00:17:30,936 --> 00:17:33,147
Remind me who is Junta again?

352
00:17:33,230 --> 00:17:34,315
Junta is Tonta.

353
00:17:34,815 --> 00:17:37,276
Oh yeah, I vaguely remember him.

354
00:17:37,359 --> 00:17:40,821
Wait, didn't he, like,
move away or something?

355
00:17:40,905 --> 00:17:42,323
Yeah, but then he moved back.

356
00:17:42,406 --> 00:17:45,117
And now he goes to school where Anzu goes.

357
00:17:45,201 --> 00:17:46,619
He had a ball game today.

358
00:17:46,702 --> 00:17:48,037
Ball game?

359
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:51,207
I don't really remember him
being the athletic type.

360
00:17:53,501 --> 00:17:55,586
-Oh?
-We're back.

361
00:17:56,879 --> 00:17:59,090
Oh, um. Hey there, everyone.

362
00:17:59,590 --> 00:18:01,509
Wow.

363
00:18:02,343 --> 00:18:03,469
Ta-da!

364
00:18:03,552 --> 00:18:06,347
-Here's Tonta!
-Or Junta Hayami!

365
00:18:07,431 --> 00:18:09,058
Huh?

366
00:18:09,141 --> 00:18:10,101
HE'S GROWN!

367
00:18:10,184 --> 00:18:12,061
He's Tonta?

368
00:18:12,603 --> 00:18:14,313
You got way too tall, man!

369
00:18:14,396 --> 00:18:16,524
I don't recall
you being such a cutie, though.

370
00:18:16,607 --> 00:18:20,986
Wait, are you the Junta Hayami?
Of Shunkan's baseball team?

371
00:18:21,070 --> 00:18:22,446
Oh, yeah.

372
00:18:22,530 --> 00:18:24,406
Really? That's so awesome!

373
00:18:24,990 --> 00:18:27,034
Didn't you have an RBI last game?

374
00:18:27,118 --> 00:18:29,578
I, I'm a total
high school baseball nut, dude.

375
00:18:29,662 --> 00:18:33,124
This is amazing. I can't believe
Tonta's a star athlete now.

376
00:18:33,207 --> 00:18:34,667
Jeez, can I get your autograph?

377
00:18:35,626 --> 00:18:37,711
I totally didn't recognize you at all.

378
00:18:37,795 --> 00:18:39,505
And you're so tall now.

379
00:18:39,588 --> 00:18:41,090
How tall are you, anyway?

380
00:18:41,173 --> 00:18:43,968
I don't know, maybe, six one?

381
00:18:44,051 --> 00:18:46,220
You must be popular.
Do you have a girlfriend?

382
00:18:46,303 --> 00:18:48,222
His girlfriend's right over here.

383
00:18:48,305 --> 00:18:50,766
I am not!

384
00:18:50,850 --> 00:18:52,309
Oh! The ginger ale stings!

385
00:18:52,393 --> 00:18:55,479
-That's so gross, bro.
-It's not like that.

386
00:18:55,563 --> 00:18:58,149
Well, you and Anzu do make sense.

387
00:18:58,232 --> 00:18:59,984
Yeah, you guys have been friends forever.

388
00:19:00,484 --> 00:19:03,654
You guys seriously crack me up.

389
00:19:03,737 --> 00:19:06,782
-Huh?
-Now you wanna be friends with him?

390
00:19:07,491 --> 00:19:10,995
Tonta, you must think
you're so much better than us now.

391
00:19:11,078 --> 00:19:12,788
Oh come on, Ryuya, please don't do this.

392
00:19:13,372 --> 00:19:16,250
I mean, you're tall,
and yeah, you're athletic.

393
00:19:17,126 --> 00:19:19,128
And on top of that, you're tall too.

394
00:19:19,211 --> 00:19:20,713
You said "tall" twice, dude.

395
00:19:21,589 --> 00:19:24,508
You just came to show off
how hot you are now, right?

396
00:19:25,092 --> 00:19:26,218
So tell me…

397
00:19:27,094 --> 00:19:30,306
Is it so bad that a person
should feel better after improving?

398
00:19:30,389 --> 00:19:31,307
Uh…

399
00:19:31,390 --> 00:19:35,102
Plus, Junta isn't doing
any of it for attention.

400
00:19:35,686 --> 00:19:39,106
He's dedicated and works hard.
He practices 24/7.

401
00:19:40,441 --> 00:19:42,443
So it's not fair to dismiss Junta

402
00:19:42,526 --> 00:19:44,904
and treat him
like he's just another pretty face.

403
00:19:45,821 --> 00:19:47,990
I'm out.

404
00:19:48,073 --> 00:19:50,451
What? Huh? Ryuya!

405
00:19:53,621 --> 00:19:55,873
Sorry guys, I'll be right back.

406
00:19:58,375 --> 00:20:00,127
Hold up, Ryuya!

407
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:03,505
I'm sorry I made a scene, okay?

408
00:20:03,589 --> 00:20:05,382
But I'm leaving, so it's fine now, right?

409
00:20:05,466 --> 00:20:08,510
Ryuya, jeez! Will you knock it off
with the moping!

410
00:20:08,594 --> 00:20:10,012
Hey!

411
00:20:11,013 --> 00:20:12,348
Just so you know.

412
00:20:12,431 --> 00:20:16,185
Not once did I ever feel bored
hanging out with you, Ryuya.

413
00:20:17,228 --> 00:20:19,271
So there's no reason to be jealous.

414
00:20:19,855 --> 00:20:22,983
Just shut up.
And don't try to make me stay.

415
00:20:23,984 --> 00:20:28,113
Anyway, you must be sick of me, right?

416
00:20:28,197 --> 00:20:32,034
Your wicked, cantankerous attitude
makes you kind of interesting.

417
00:20:32,117 --> 00:20:34,828
You were super devious
when we play games too.

418
00:20:34,912 --> 00:20:38,082
Are those supposed to be compliments?
Jeez, Anzu.

419
00:20:38,958 --> 00:20:42,127
Listen, I know I made it awkward
for you to stay

420
00:20:42,211 --> 00:20:43,587
because of how I spoke up.

421
00:20:44,088 --> 00:20:46,548
But those guys will understand.

422
00:20:47,758 --> 00:20:50,094
And don't worry,
this doesn't make me hate you.

423
00:20:50,177 --> 00:20:51,470
We can still be friends.

424
00:20:56,392 --> 00:21:00,020
Oh man, this is crazy.
You really haven't changed at all.

425
00:21:00,104 --> 00:21:03,774
What? I mean, I'm a little more womanly
at this point, right?

426
00:21:03,857 --> 00:21:05,609
That's not what I meant.

427
00:21:05,693 --> 00:21:09,363
I didn't think I had feelings anymore
because it's been years.

428
00:21:10,698 --> 00:21:13,784
But I, um, I lied before.

429
00:21:14,535 --> 00:21:16,120
My preschool teacher.

430
00:21:17,246 --> 00:21:20,624
My real first love was, it was you.

431
00:21:22,501 --> 00:21:24,003
I mean, um…

432
00:21:25,379 --> 00:21:27,548
-I still really like--
-Sorry, no way.

433
00:21:27,631 --> 00:21:30,342
Hey, at least let me finish!

434
00:21:30,426 --> 00:21:32,094
Sorry, I couldn't hold it in.

435
00:21:32,177 --> 00:21:36,098
Anyway, I'd never be with someone
who'd date two girls at once!

436
00:21:36,181 --> 00:21:39,476
You have a girlfriend, and now
you're telling me that you like me too?

437
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:41,895
Uh… Uh, but well, we--

438
00:21:42,479 --> 00:21:44,189
we went to different schools, Anzu!

439
00:21:44,898 --> 00:21:46,025
What was I supposed to do?

440
00:21:46,108 --> 00:21:48,319
She was really sweet and she lives close.

441
00:21:48,902 --> 00:21:50,821
Seriously, dude?

442
00:21:50,904 --> 00:21:54,325
But I… I thought about you
the whole time I was with her.

443
00:21:54,408 --> 00:21:57,911
And another girl asked me out
and I thought she'd help me forget you.

444
00:21:58,412 --> 00:22:01,498
Anyway, I messed up.
And I looked like a cheater.

445
00:22:01,582 --> 00:22:03,125
You're a trash bag.

446
00:22:03,208 --> 00:22:06,211
Gah! Thank you for being real.

447
00:22:06,295 --> 00:22:09,757
Gah, but how come
I still like you after all this?

448
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:12,426
You're cold, you're not sexy.

449
00:22:12,509 --> 00:22:14,345
You shoot ginger ale out of your nose.

450
00:22:14,428 --> 00:22:16,430
The ginger ale was a total act of God.

451
00:22:17,056 --> 00:22:17,973
Hey.

452
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:20,934
Do I really not stand a chance?

453
00:22:24,313 --> 00:22:25,898
I appreciate how you feel.

454
00:22:26,398 --> 00:22:27,566
I really do.

455
00:22:27,649 --> 00:22:29,985
But I wanna be with someone
who wouldn't cheat on me

456
00:22:30,069 --> 00:22:31,528
just because we're apart.

457
00:22:32,863 --> 00:22:35,866
Do you mean, someone like Tonta?

458
00:22:35,949 --> 00:22:38,118
Huh? He totally nailed it!

459
00:22:38,202 --> 00:22:41,705
No, not at all. I don't think
Junta sees me like that anyway.

460
00:22:41,789 --> 00:22:43,874
What? Are you really that dumb?

461
00:22:43,957 --> 00:22:46,627
That's been totally obvious
for eons, Anzu!

462
00:22:48,253 --> 00:22:51,590
Anyway, you and I are friends
and nothing more, Ryuya!

463
00:22:51,673 --> 00:22:54,802
You're too straightforward!
My heart's torn to shreds!

464
00:22:54,885 --> 00:22:56,303
Huh?

465
00:22:56,387 --> 00:22:58,263
Ryuya just got rejected!

466
00:22:58,347 --> 00:23:00,432
Oh jeez, I couldn't hold it in anymore!

467
00:23:00,516 --> 00:23:03,811
Hey, that's messed up!
Don't laugh about my unrequited love!

468
00:23:04,603 --> 00:23:06,063
Now, I'm ruined.

469
00:23:06,146 --> 00:23:09,191
They already make fun of me
because they know I like you.

470
00:23:09,274 --> 00:23:11,276
It's not like
your first love was a disgrace.

471
00:23:12,194 --> 00:23:14,321
You guys came over
because you were worried, right?

472
00:23:14,405 --> 00:23:15,739
Yeah.

473
00:23:16,573 --> 00:23:19,952
I was worried
because I thought I made you feel bad.

474
00:23:20,494 --> 00:23:22,663
How could you possibly care about me?

475
00:23:22,746 --> 00:23:24,581
Now I feel really petty.

476
00:23:24,665 --> 00:23:26,959
-Well, you should. You are.
-Just shut up!

477
00:23:27,543 --> 00:23:28,627
I'm sorry.

478
00:23:28,710 --> 00:23:30,921
I just got jealous
but don't worry about it.

479
00:23:32,548 --> 00:23:33,882
Anzu got it right.

480
00:23:33,966 --> 00:23:35,926
You did a lot to improve yourself.

481
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:38,178
That's hella impressive.

482
00:23:38,929 --> 00:23:40,472
Thanks, Ryuya.

483
00:23:41,014 --> 00:23:43,183
Hey, you don't have
to thank me, dude.

484
00:23:45,018 --> 00:23:47,938
All right, let's go back.
Everyone's waiting.

485
00:23:48,021 --> 00:23:51,066
Both Ryuya and Junta?
You're so popular, Anzu.

486
00:23:51,150 --> 00:23:52,901
Junta doesn't feel that way
about me.

487
00:23:53,735 --> 00:23:58,198
I just gotta lean into
the heroine oblivious twist feelings act.

488
00:23:59,491 --> 00:24:00,576
Tonta, wait up.

489
00:24:01,577 --> 00:24:05,289
I actually lied about something
a long time ago.

490
00:24:05,956 --> 00:24:07,166
Hmm?

491
00:24:07,249 --> 00:24:08,459
Hey, Tonta.

492
00:24:08,959 --> 00:24:12,004
Anzu said she doesn't wanna play
Cat Ranger with you anymore,

493
00:24:12,504 --> 00:24:14,631
because she's playing it
with all of us now.

494
00:24:16,758 --> 00:24:17,926
Okay.

495
00:24:18,010 --> 00:24:21,763
That was how I kept you
from being able to play with her.

496
00:24:22,598 --> 00:24:24,224
And because of that,

497
00:24:24,308 --> 00:24:29,146
you didn't have time to talk to her
and you moved away, shortly after.

498
00:24:30,481 --> 00:24:31,315
I see.

499
00:24:32,649 --> 00:24:33,817
Well, what a relief.

500
00:24:34,318 --> 00:24:37,237
I thought it was because Anzu
didn't wanna play with me anymore.

501
00:24:37,738 --> 00:24:40,824
Come on, man!
Why the hell aren't you mad at me?

502
00:24:40,908 --> 00:24:43,869
Uh, well, it's, it's all
in the past for me.

503
00:24:43,952 --> 00:24:46,079
And anyway,
I get to hang out with Anzu now.

504
00:24:47,581 --> 00:24:50,375
This whole time, you felt guilty about it.

505
00:24:51,126 --> 00:24:53,253
This guy's way too nice.

506
00:24:53,337 --> 00:24:56,048
Well, I wanna apologize for that too.

507
00:24:56,632 --> 00:25:00,552
Sorry, but it's not like I've given up
on Anzu, all right?

508
00:25:00,636 --> 00:25:02,721
-Well, I, um--
-You like her, right?

509
00:25:05,599 --> 00:25:08,227
It's totally obvious, man. Let's go.

510
00:25:11,647 --> 00:25:15,526
Ryuya!
Congratulations on your heartbreak!

511
00:25:15,609 --> 00:25:17,402
All right! Let's do a round

512
00:25:17,486 --> 00:25:19,446
where we dedicate
all the heartbreak songs to Ryuya!

513
00:25:20,781 --> 00:25:21,615
BREAKUP SONG RANKING

514
00:25:21,698 --> 00:25:23,200
You guys, what?

515
00:25:23,283 --> 00:25:25,494
This is seriously so messed up!

516
00:25:25,577 --> 00:25:26,411
BREAKUP SONG RANKING

517
00:25:27,454 --> 00:25:29,039
A fanfare, please!

518
00:25:29,122 --> 00:25:31,542
And a big congratulations!

519
00:25:31,625 --> 00:25:33,544
Did you fall for my little trick?

520
00:25:33,627 --> 00:25:36,588
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

521
00:25:36,672 --> 00:25:40,342
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

522
00:25:40,425 --> 00:25:43,095
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

523
00:25:43,178 --> 00:25:45,681
Don't just let things be! Come on!

524
00:25:45,764 --> 00:25:48,141
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

525
00:25:48,225 --> 00:25:50,143
So I can make sure I get paid.

526
00:26:16,712 --> 00:26:19,548
I'll never give myself up to these ikemen!

527
00:26:19,631 --> 00:26:23,010
That's what you say now,
but I know you'll give in eventually!

